==English==

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|head=[[bust]] [[chops]]}}

# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To [[nag]]; to [[berate]] or [[hound]] in an effort to elicit action.
#: The boss has been '''busting chops''' all day.
#: The boss '''busted''' our '''chops''' all week.

====Usage notes====
''To bust (someone's) balls'' is an alternative version that is not suitable for formal or business usage (here ''balls'' = [[testicle]]s).

